// "[Permanent] endures N" [CR#701.63a]: the rules instruct the permanent
// itself, so a card hands the action to it (`act(thisCreature, endure(1))`)
// and the wrapper records that permanent; written with no such handoff, the
// source permanent endures. Inside the handoff `actor` is the permanent, and
// "that permanent's controller" does the rest, so the body hands it on to
// `controllerOf(actor)`: they create an N/N white Spirit creature token unless
// they put N +1/+1 counters on "that permanent", the enduring one, still in
// view. The "unless" is the controller's own choice between the two. Endure
// 0 does nothing, neither counters nor a token [CR#701.63b], which is the
// rules' to apply, as connive 0's is (`conniveN`).
KeywordAction(
    name: "endure",
    params: [Amount],
    spelling: "endure <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "endure",
        frame_set: MeasureComplement,
    ),
    body: act(
        controllerOf(actor),
        chooseOne(
            putCounters(Param(0), p1p1Counter, that(Permanent)),
            createToken(creatureTokenOf(Param(0), Param(0), [White], [spirit])),
        ),
    ),
)
